[00:18.92]There is a book that by its many pages,
[00:24.78]Brings peace and joy and hope to humankind.
[00:30.70]Its wondrous thoughts are charged with such great power;
[00:36.92]It brings life to the “dead,” sight to the “blind.”
[00:42.72]That precious book is God’s own Holy Bible.
[00:48.74]Its words were penned by men whom God inspired,
[00:54.50]By men who truly loved their God Jehovah,
[01:01.00]And by his holy spirit they were fired.
[01:23.60]They wrote a record true of God’s creations,
[01:29.40]How by his might this universe appeared.
[01:35.62]They also told how man at first was sinless
[01:42.04]But how his Paradise then disappeared.
[01:47.90]They further told about a certain angel
[01:53.52]Who challenged God and spurned his sov’reignty.
[02:00.28]That challenge led to sin and man’s great sorrow,
[02:06.26]But soon will come Jehovah’s victory.
[02:12.80]The time has come with reason for rejoicing:
[02:31.26]Jehovah rules by his anointed King.
[02:37.26]So now we preach the good news of the Kingdom
[02:42.98]And share the hope of blessings it will bring.
[02:49.58]Within his book are found these cheerful tidings;
[02:55.72]A sacred banquet feast on which to feed.
[03:01.94]It offers peace beyond all human thinking;
[03:08.02]This Living Treasure beckons all to read.
